WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.510 --> 00:00:09.540
As descendants of apes, there remains a lingering
ape in all of us that continues to provoke

00:00:09.540 --> 00:00:13.590
many of our behavioral and social traits.

00:00:13.590 --> 00:00:23.000
In particular, one of the most apparent characteristics
that we continue to share with our ape relatives

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:28.310
is the desire for the social position of alpha
male.

00:00:28.310 --> 00:00:31.730
In the ape world, the alpha male is everything.

00:00:31.730 --> 00:00:39.440
He gets his pick of mates, ownership of territory,
and control over his group.

00:00:39.440 --> 00:00:46.560
All of which are not far from the same desired
interests of most men, and often women, in

00:00:46.560 --> 00:00:49.109
the modern human world.

00:00:49.109 --> 00:00:52.960
So what does it take to become an alpha?

00:00:52.960 --> 00:01:00.780
In the ape world, there are several factors
at play that determine who becomes the alpha.

00:01:00.780 --> 00:01:09.440
They include things like size, loudness, and
the ability to dominate others as unequals.

00:01:09.440 --> 00:01:15.710
In the human world, becoming this sort of
domineering alpha involves most of the same

00:01:15.710 --> 00:01:17.610
factors.

00:01:17.610 --> 00:01:25.790
We can intimidate other humans into submission
through size, intensity, and force.

00:01:25.790 --> 00:01:32.610
And if we live with these behaviors, we can
become this same sort of alpha.

00:01:32.610 --> 00:01:38.350
But how does the function of this position
compare in human world?

00:01:38.350 --> 00:01:45.970
How do the differences between humans and
apes weigh in on the value of such a domineering

00:01:45.970 --> 00:01:49.909
behavioral archetype?

00:01:49.909 --> 00:01:56.450
The principal difference between human and
ape is the depth of our consciousness.

00:01:56.450 --> 00:02:04.590
It is still unclear as to what degree our
consciousness extends beyond our ape relatives,

00:02:04.590 --> 00:02:11.560
but the majority of researchers and philosophers
can agree that we have a largely superior

00:02:11.560 --> 00:02:20.219
ability to exhibit a consciousness that allows
for self-awareness and critical reflection.

00:02:20.219 --> 00:02:28.010
We have passed a threshold of mental complexity
where we can now think about thinking.

00:02:28.010 --> 00:02:34.430
We can consider our intentions and how our
actions may affect others.

00:02:34.430 --> 00:02:41.560
We can take it one step further and consider
how others’ reactions to our actions will

00:02:41.560 --> 00:02:46.150
make us feel and think about ourselves.

00:02:46.150 --> 00:02:53.540
And we can employ reason, empathy, and morality
to act accordingly.

00:02:53.540 --> 00:03:01.299
As a result, even though we may still have
an ape in us who hungers to be that of a domineering

00:03:01.299 --> 00:03:08.959
alpha, our higher human consciousness caters
to a different type of alpha.

00:03:08.959 --> 00:03:17.010
For example, being an ape-like alpha and getting
the pick of any woman may sound appealing,

00:03:17.010 --> 00:03:23.689
but it does not really help with the pairing
of the right man with the right woman.

00:03:23.689 --> 00:03:30.239
In the ape world, the goal of the alpha is
to have sex and reproduce with as many mates

00:03:30.239 --> 00:03:34.090
as possible, not to form intimate relationships.

00:03:34.090 --> 00:03:39.260
But in the human world, we want relationships.

00:03:39.260 --> 00:03:46.079
We want to find partners who we can exchange
love with and help balance out each other’s

00:03:46.079 --> 00:03:47.079
lives.

00:03:47.079 --> 00:03:54.139
And in the context of friendships, behaving
as a dominating and forceful individual may

00:03:54.139 --> 00:04:01.279
acquire you yes-men and followers but not
necessarily any true friends, because rarely

00:04:01.279 --> 00:04:08.760
does anyone want to continue in a long-term
friendship comprised of dominance, fear, and

00:04:08.760 --> 00:04:11.299
hierarchy.

00:04:11.299 --> 00:04:18.109
In a true friendship, we want mutual trust,
respect, and affinity.

00:04:18.109 --> 00:04:26.370
Therefore, we must consider how our primal
desire to be a domineering alpha affects our

00:04:26.370 --> 00:04:30.630
life and appropriately regulate it.

00:04:30.630 --> 00:04:38.790
Our ape self is constantly lingering within
us and it is not simple or easy to overcome.

00:04:38.790 --> 00:04:47.190
But by using our faculty for higher consciousness
to understand our behaviors and their affects,

00:04:47.190 --> 00:04:53.470
we can construct and execute a new refined
concept of alpha.

00:04:53.470 --> 00:04:56.670
A conscious alpha.

00:04:56.670 --> 00:05:03.470
We did not evolve over millions of years to
merely continue to perpetuate the behaviors

00:05:03.470 --> 00:05:06.950
of our lesser ancestors.

00:05:06.950 --> 00:05:13.310
Becoming a true human alpha involves being
able to adapt to the terms of the current

00:05:13.310 --> 00:05:15.590
human condition.

00:05:15.590 --> 00:05:22.870
To infuse rationality, self-awareness, and
empathy into our behavior.

00:05:22.870 --> 00:05:29.280
More important than being big and loud and
forceful, is being someone who can exhibit

00:05:29.280 --> 00:05:33.720
compassion and reason.

00:05:33.720 --> 00:05:51.630
Someone who is comfortable enough with themselves
to not feel a need to always compete for a

00:05:51.630 --> 00:05:52.630
sense of self worth.

00:05:52.630 --> 00:05:56.000
Someone who is conscious enough to practice
control over their mind and body.

00:05:56.000 --> 00:06:01.570
We humans function better off of solidarity,
compassion, and intellect, and so it is these

00:06:01.570 --> 00:06:12.020
qualities that we must attend to if we wish
to truly be a prevailing human.

